/*	Welcome to Terrains.json, world's best json object hash/keys since 0xD!

	Ultima V base is a Total Conversion basemod. Mod explorers should find interest in this mods' internals!
	  ("TC" mod="total conversion") Mod_params: isBaseRuleset
	
	The mod as a whole includes:
	  ✅ TileSet
	  ✅ UnitSet
	  ✅ Edges
	  ✅ Map
	  ✅ Skin

	# Base terrains
	    Mostly the same as G&K, highlighting familiar tiles:
		Flatland =~ Plains+<features/Grass>, used primarily for Paths
		Surf: Usually found between Coast and Ocean as a water mid-body, originally subbed as Lakes
		+ Land&Water de-edging: edge sprites are removed in cloned base tiles, to de-edge shorelines for blending decors.
	        - "waterline" sprite set, universal terrain sprite quads for either land or water source
	        - the source type ensures correct base terrain behavior
		+ Rough Ocean: Vis blocking ocean tiles, w/ specific buff/de-buffs
	        - new base water terrain not in original U5
	        - gameplay characteristics extensively observed in mod Z2, found to add real fun over plain "flat water"!
	        - will create vis and M differentials, ship type modifiers
		? Lakes: May add specific Lake terrain for Lost Lake etc, surf works fine atm
		Tundra|Snow: Only one default instance atm, glass sword
	# Natural Wonders
		No G&K NW's.
		+ Ultima V specific NW's:
		> Dungeons, both main castles, Codex, others
	# TerrainFeatures
	    Migrating TF's from Ultima-tileset mod and G&K:
		Swamp =~ Marsh, basically the same
		+ Brush: light vegetation
		+ Woods =~ Forest
		Forest: Heavier density
		Thicket =~ Jungle, more apt naming for a European fantasy setting
		- Ice,Atoll
		? Flood plains, possibly useful for bridges/ as an underbody TF
		+ bridges/, features/
	# TerrainDecor
	    What is "TerrainDecor" (TD)? A sub-class of TFs, for decorating tiles:
	    + Can be layered before or after a TF, extending tile graphics versatility
		+ paths/  - basic decor, road entity is manually overlaid
		+ rivers/ - deviation from Unciv, where rivers are an entity type that act as boundary terrain
	              - in U5, rivers are TF's with associated uniques, gaining the breadth of uniques control
	              - entity type _rivers_ have been converted into map editor "meshes" for guiding/revealing tile boundariess
    # TerrainDetails
        What are "TerrainDetails" (TL)? A final sub-class of TFs, for tile aesthetics:
        + non-modifier TF layer, no gameplay effect
        + adds finer details for visual enhancement - presently hill and sand
        + bridges map scale (1:4) to (1:1) for various areas using sprite quads
	# Special assets
		features/ - for ruleVariant terrain render layering, or other indirect tile render assets
		editor/ - useful map editor related sprites for better mapdev
		  We implement some new editor techniques for advanced map creation. See the Editor section.
	# Legacy
		Assets from Ultima-tileset|retroset and G&K that are being replaced tile by tile. Map migration!
		It was decided not to rebuild the whole map, instead, recolor replacement tiles, swap in new tiles/entities.
		  This process itself was an immense undertaking. Several new techniques emerged from this effort.

//// internal Terrains.json block notes ////

